# Bard Necro Enhanced: sustain, bard control, necro burst, opener and damage rotation.
# Design, cooldown model and every barding number: blueprint/bard-necro-handbook.html
# (design in part 5, mechanics in part 2).
# Needs: Discordance, Peacemaking and Provocation trained (the song round robin parks on a
# missing one), an instrument in the backpack, a necromancer book, and reagents.
# The hotbar's own Auto-Renew must be OFF for every ability this loop drives: it spends
# the same symbols, cheapest first.
# cooldowns.xml carries every bar this loop reads: music, song, disco, peace/provo, magic
# arrow, harm, fireball, lightning, heal pot, reflect and walk. The names are lowercase
# and the glossary is blueprint/overheads.html.
# A fight is a hostile inside target_range. In a fight: Discordance, Peacemaking, the
# necro burst, the opener, the proc core, the filler and Poison Strike. On the walk: the
# mushroom, the self buffs, Spell Siphon, the bard song and Vampiric Embrace.
# Warmode is the player's manual window: our casts, the bard skills, the self buffs,
# Create Food, Corpse Skin and Evil Omen stand down. Cures, heals, potions, the mushroom
# and Blood Oath keep running.
# Herding is off: the slot went to Resisting Spells on 2026-09-27. Add tamer/herding to the
# blocks when it comes back.
# Hotkeys: Drink Cure, > Smart Heal/Cure Self, Drink Heal, > Greater Heal/Cure Self,
#          Cancel Current Target, Drink Refresh, Drink Strength, Drink Agility, Drink Magic Resist,
#          Blood Oath, Corpse Skin, Evil Omen, > Interrupt, Poison Strike, Eat Magic Mushroom,
#          Target Self, Vampiric Embrace.
# Generated from recipe/bard-necro-enhanced-recipe.razor by util/build-scripts.py. Edit module/ and recipe/, not this file.


# ========================================================================================
# CONFIG
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# module/base.razor
#
#   config__chatty
#      1 shows the optional overheads. Warnings show either way.
#
#   config__sysmsg
#      1 writes Journal diagnostics. A block that writes one says so in its comments.
#
#   config__clear_at_start
#      What Play does first (conventions 02.D).
#        0  nothing: a cursor or a cast the player holds at Play is kept
#        1  clear the client queues, the journal and the ignore list
#
#   config__use_magery
#      1 uses Magery: the Cure and heal agents, the reagent reads and the buffs. At 0
#      potions and bandages still go out.
#
#   config__use_potions
#      1 uses potions: cure, heal, Refresh and the stat potions.
#
#   config__walk_guard
#      Our casts and the walk bar.
#        0  cast while walking, for a fight where there is no better moment to wait for
#        1  wait while the walk bar runs, so a step does not break the cast
#
#   config__warmode_is_manual
#      Whose warmode it is.
#        0  ours: our casts ignore it
#        1  the player's manual control window: our casts and the food stand down while it
#           is on. Potions and bandages still go out
#      > This loop: config__warmode_is_manual 1 (default 0).
#      > The player casts by hand in warmode: our casts, buffs and food stand down then.
#
#   config__recover_in_warmode
#      With warmode_is_manual 1, what the recovery casts (cure, heal, light Heal) do in
#      warmode.
#        0  stand down with the rest
#        1  keep going, so only the other casts wait for the player
#      > This loop: config__recover_in_warmode 1 (default 0).
#      > What keeps the character alive keeps running in warmode.
#
#   config__use_bandages
#      1 uses bandages. At 0 recovery/light-heal stands in.
#      > This loop: config__use_bandages 0 (default 1).
#      > No bandages in this loop: the light Heal agent stands in for them.
#
#   config__heal_skill_min
#      Healing must be above this to bandage. At or below it recovery/light-heal stands
#      in.
#
#   config__settle_first
#      What a pass does first.
#        0  reads the state at once. Potions still go out while a spell is casting
#        1  waits for the item queue and any cast to finish
#      > This loop: config__settle_first 1 (default 0).
#      > Anything already in flight finishes before the pass reads state.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__chatty 1
@setvar! config__sysmsg 1
@setvar! config__clear_at_start 1
@setvar! config__use_magery 1
@setvar! config__use_potions 1
@setvar! config__walk_guard 1
@setvar! config__warmode_is_manual 1
@setvar! config__recover_in_warmode 1
@setvar! config__use_bandages 0
@setvar! config__heal_skill_min 0
@setvar! config__settle_first 1


